The original contract and early addendum contain contradictory statements; this clarification supersedes them for this bead and records existing source behavior, not a weakened ticket contract. No owner waiver is granted. A complete exact pendingticket match includingattempt/capacity/seq/key passes ownership. Genuine oldticketclassification requires0<attempt<pending.attempt, same run/step/action/capacity, canonicalkey,seq<=pending.seq and returnsStaleAttempt before mutation. Missingrun=>RunNotFound. All other forged/missingpendingticketcases=>InvalidActionCompletion. It is impossible for a ticket to be a full exactmatch and simultaneously differinattempt/capacity. The addendum's sentence suggesting this is wrong and withdrawn. Public API tests must not fabricate malformed pendingauthority to force lowerlevelAttemptBeyondMax.

